BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315230524@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T042427Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260920T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260920T130000
SUMMARY:Toronto's Art Deco 1929-1939: VOLUME 1 and 2 (SPECIAL EXTENDED TOU
 R)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nArt Deco is al
 l around us.\n\nStreamlined Modern or Art Modern are two other fascinating
  ways to say the same thing. Whichever way you plan on saying it\, Art Dec
 o buildings tell a rich story of optimism and positivity during one of the
  most darkest decades in history\, the great depression of the 1930s!\n\nT
 his walking tour explores our built environment of our downtown core. Toro
 nto Stock Exchange built in 1937\, along with the Royal York Hotel and the
  Canada Permanent Trust Company are prime examples. But others line Spadin
 a Avenue during the challenging years of the depression\, but also during 
 the tensions which were bubbling in the Garment Industry. Art Deco buildin
 gs were centre stage!\n\nThese buildings tell a story that goes beyond sty
 le into the heart of the Toronto story itself!\n\nBuilt at the height of t
 he roaring 1920s and 1930s\, the bubble was about to burst however\, and t
 he depression was just settling in. But a new style would set the tone\, a
 nd it was called Art Deco!\n\nToronto built some of its most enduring buil
 dings\, and left a built legacy of Art Deco during the 1930s which should 
 be treasured and protected. Losing any of these treasures would surly be a
  loss to the community. They tell a rich and inviting story about the grow
 th of Canada\, and Toronto!\n\nThis walking tour is for all walking levels
 . Please dress for the season\, and hope to see you there.\n\nPlease meet 
 under the **clock tower** of the Queens Quay Terminal at 207 Queens Quay W
 est on the south side just west of York Street! We end on Spadina and Rich
 mond Street!\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\n\\*\
 \* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your sp
 ace for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**toro
 ntohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315230
 524/
