BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315367626@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T042427Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T140000
SUMMARY:Ireland Park\, Queen's Wharf\, and 1847 Irish Potato Famine
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Explo
 rer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tour
 s\, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or 
 for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the tic
 ket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to th
 e following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThis special
  historical walking tour discusses the Irish Potato Famine in great detail
 \, and the implications for Toronto in 1847.\n\nStarting the walking tour 
 near Ireland Park just east of Bathurst Quay we take a deep dive into the 
 events that saw thousands of people head west to Toronto in 1847! A truly 
 global event! A life changing event for those caught up in the famine in I
 reland and Toronto itself. Toronto was never the same after\, and impacted
  the future of the city for nearly a century.\n\nBut the stories surroundi
 ng Ireland Park are not the only stories from this era. This tour looks at
  the Potato Famine with a different lens. We end at the corner of King and
  John streets at the site of the Fever Sheds.\n\nThis extensive tour begin
 s in **Little Norway Park** adjacent to Queen's Quay West\, at the foot of
  Bathurst Street\, and ends at King Street and John Street!\n\nThis tour i
 s for all walking levels. Please dress for the season.\n\nThis walk has a 
 ticket price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-trans
 fer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-tra
 nsfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315367
 626/
