CREATED:20260618T143032Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260618T143032Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315426128@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T042427Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T140000
SUMMARY:Historic Port Credit and Mississauga (ONLY DATE FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThe location w
 as a well known meeting place between the indigenous and and the white tra
 ders\, and the Credit River was known to them as Missinhe. In 1720\, a tra
 ding post was built and the area known today as Mississauga entered record
 ed history!\n\nThe first building was English built in 1798 on the east ba
 nk of the river. Lieutenant Governor Simcoe had ordered some sort of rest 
 stop for travellers\, but was destroyed by fire years later!\n\nMississaug
 a came of age in the early 1970s with the amalgamation of several towns in
  the area. However\, near disaster brought the community together and Miss
 issauga started to grow. Today it is one of the fastest growing cities in 
 Canada and growth remains brisk. Mississauga is a fascinating city to disc
 over and explore. You will enjoy this walk\, for that I am sure\, and I'm 
 very rarely wrong\, just saying.\n\nThis walking tour is for all walking l
 evels and fitness skills. Please dress for the season and bring water. And
  remember to bring your love of history.\n\nThis tour begins under the lig
 hthouse at 105 Lakeshore Road West in Mississauga overlooking the Credit R
 iver. The tour returns to the start location after the walk!\n\nThis tour 
 has a ticket price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e
 -transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can
  e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com*
 *
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315426
 128/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260626T115006Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260626T115006Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315426185@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T042427Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T170000
SUMMARY:Historic Cooksville - MISSISSAUGA (ONLY DATE FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nCooksville was
  the real heart of old Toronto Township. But it started out as Harrisville
  after the original settler\, and was a major transit hub and stagecoach l
 ine through the heart of Upper Canada. The Dundas highway linked the capit
 al of York with the hinterland\, and the western ends of the empire to the
  west and southwest towards today's Windsor.\n\nCooksville was also the ho
 me of a European Grand Duchess\, I guess you will just have to take the to
 ur to find out that answer and that fascinating story. Here's a clue she a
 lso lived on Gerrard Street in Toronto and I talk about it in my Riverdale
  walk. Or if you think you know drop me a line. Interesting indeed?\n\nThi
 s is a an area that has plenty of history\, but not all that well known. L
 et's explore Mississauga together. Plenty to learn here.\n\nThis walking t
 our is for all walking levels and fitness skills. Please dress for the sea
 son and bring water. And remember to bring your love of history.\n\nThis t
 our begins at the southeast corner of Dundas Street East and Hurontario in
  Mississauga. The tour returns to the start location after the walk!\n\nTh
 e ticket price is $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-tra
 nsfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-t
 ransfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
