SUMMARY:History of Aviation 3: The Ghost of Flight 401? (LECTURE ON THE GO
 )
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\nWe have an amazing "Lecture on the Go" series for 2026. New
  topics and fascinating stories abound! Join us and learn about the world 
 and keep active and warm and cool during the winter and summer months!\n\n
 I started this walking classroom when we were under that horrible cloud ca
 lled Covid. This series was popular and helped people get back into societ
 y and life. **This is part three of the Aviation series that will debut in
  August 2026 with the Lecture on the disaster at Tenerife**!\n\nThe "Lectu
 re on the Go" Series is open to members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMB
 ERSHIP PASS\, it's free for those members. If you wish to attend a lecture
  and you are not a yearly pass member then the price **per** lecture is $2
 0.00.\n\nIn this third part of *History of Aviation: Was there really a gh
 ost of fight 401? Lecture on the Go* series\, we explore one of the most e
 xtraordinary stories in modern aviation history. A true story that morphed
  into a decades long investigation\, and put a spotlight on the airline in
 dustry itself. The events surrounding Eastern Airlines Flight 401 is fasci
 nating\, and sounds a bit like a modern horror story\, but it's true. I ca
 n't wait to find out your take on this modern ghost story.\n\nEastern Air 
 Lines Flight 401 is one of the most famous and influential aviation disast
 ers in history. The flight crashed late at night on December 29\, 1972\, w
 hile approaching Miami\, Florida\, after departing from New York’s JFK A
 irport. The aircraft was a new Lockheed L-1011 TriStar\, one of the most t
 echnologically advanced airliners of its kind.\n\nThe accident happened du
 ring the final stages of landing. The crew became distracted by a malfunct
 ioning landing gear indicator light in the cockpit. While they focused on 
 the small bulb issue\, the aircraft descended without the pilots fully rea
 lizing it. The autopilot had been unintentionally disconnected\, and the p
 lane drifted lower and lower into the dark Florida Everglades.\n\nAt 11:42
  p.m.\, Flight 401 crashed into the Everglades about 18 miles northwest of
  Miami Airport. The impact destroyed much of the aircraft across the swamp
 y terrain. Of the 176 people on board\, 101 died\, including the captain a
 nd first officer\, while 75 survived. Rescue operations were difficult bec
 ause of the remote location\, darkness\, mud\, and water.\n\nThe tragedy b
 ecame historically important because it demonstrated a major danger in avi
 ation known as “crew distraction.” The aircraft itself was functioning
 \, but the crew lost awareness of altitude while concentrating on a relati
 vely minor problem. The crash helped push airlines and regulators toward i
 mproved cockpit procedures. Many aviation historians consider Flight 401 a
  turning point in how airlines train pilots.\n\nThe accident also became f
 amous in popular culture because of stories surrounding “Ghosts of Fligh
 t 401.” According to airline legends from the 1970s\, some Eastern emplo
 yees claimed to see apparitions of Captain Bob Loft and Flight Engineer Do
 n Repo aboard other Eastern aircraft after parts from the crashed plane we
 re reused. While there is no evidence supporting these claims\, the storie
 s became widely known through books\, documentaries\, and movies.\n\nIn th
 is lecture on the Go\,\nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\\*Philosop
 hy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (August 2026)\n\
 \*Philosophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lam
 a - (July 2026)\nThe 1977 Disaster at Tenerife - (August 2026)\nLegacy of 
 Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North America - (Septembe
 r 2026)\nHistory of Aviation (September 2026)\nHistory of Aviation 3: Was 
 there a ghost of flight 401?\n\nSo book your plans now!\n\nThis event is f
 or all levels and walkers\, there are a few steps here and there to naviga
 te\, but mostly on one level. This event in a non-walking event.\n\nThe le
 cture begins on the steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay 
 Street and Queen Street West\, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per perso
 n\, but **free with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please
  e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You c
 an e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.co
 m**
